# {{TITLE}}

This project was generated by the Miniquad browser starter generator
(`scripts/create-browser-project.mjs` in the Miniquad repository).
It does not depend on, or live inside, that repository at run time.

## Prerequisites

Developers need:

- Rust and Cargo (https://rustup.rs).
- The `wasm32-unknown-unknown` Rust target: `rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown`.
- Node.js, to run the build and serve scripts (builtins only, no packages).

End users of the deployed output need only a browser. They do not need
Rust or Node.js.

## Commands

| Step | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Build the WASM application | `node scripts/build.mjs` |
| Serve the output locally | `node scripts/serve.mjs --port 8080` |
| Serve from a subpath | `node scripts/serve.mjs --port 8080 --base /my-app` |
| Deploy | Copy the `web/` directory to a static host. |

`web/` is the self-contained output directory. It has the HTML host
page, the application WASM, the matching browser bridge files, and a
`MANIFEST.json` recording the exact source revision and file hashes
used at generation time.

## Source provenance

See `web/MANIFEST.json` for the Miniquad source revision and the
SHA-256 hash of each copied browser file.
